# Request
# Which map area (room) contains this point, and which named sublocations
# (furniture/placement poses) of that area are closest to it. The point may be
# stamped in any TF frame; nav_central transforms it to the map frame first.
#
# Single source of truth for "where is this?": vision and task_manager should
# call this instead of re-implementing point-in-polygon against their own copy
# of areas.json (only the active map's areas_<MAP_NAME>.json is authoritative).

geometry_msgs/PointStamped point
float32 max_sublocation_distance   # meters; <= 0 uses the default (1.5)
---
#Response
bool success
string area                        # "" when the point is in no area polygon
string[] sublocations              # names in `area`, sorted by XY distance
float32[] distances                # meters, same order as sublocations
bool in_house                      # inside ANY area polygon
string error
